Sval: Keep animated content under an SVG mask off the CPU every frame

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2038325 (mozilla-central 2c558f13263b,
Firefox 158) with its regression fix from Bug 2087421 (mozilla-central
7a7d99a492f4, Firefox 161), folded into one change. Bug 2087421 is
adapted: its hunks in IsItemProbablyActive and the middle-of-list
threshold in Grouper::ConstructGroups are applied to ESR 153's code,
which has no simple-clip-shape early return for masks and no relaxed
active threshold. Its browser-chrome test,
gfx/tests/browser/browser_svg_masked_animation.js, is left out: it
sets prefs and reads a "WebRender blob images" profiler marker that
ESR 153 does not have. Bug 2038325's reftests are kept.

Inside an <svg>, a masked group only left the blob image when a child
had to be active. With a luminance mask over a large <image> and an
animated sibling, every frame rasterized the masked image and the mask
again on the CPU, which keeps the GPU process at full CPU on Google
results pages with an AI overview. Letting a child that should be
active pull the group out of the blob keeps the mask image cached and
lets the image stay a WebRender primitive.

Taken alone, that change also split masked groups for animated
transforms over blob content, which made lottie-style SVG animations
under clip-paths re-render so slowly that pages could barely scroll.
Bug 2087421 gives animated transforms their own activity level,
ShouldForAnimation, below Should: it still splits an unmasked blob as
before, while a masked group leaves the blob only for native content
or required activity.

diff --git a/gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp b/gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp
index 64b3553fc..dce580e20 100644
--- a/gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp
+++ b/gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp
@@ -1088,12 +1088,12 @@ enum class ItemActivity : uint8_t {
   /// Could be active if it has no layerization cost.
   /// Typically active if first of an item group.
   Could = 1,
+  /// Should be active for animation unless affected by a complex mask.
+  ShouldForAnimation = 2,
   /// Should be active unless something external makes that less useful.
-  /// For example if the item is affected by a complex mask, it remains
-  /// inactive.
-  Should = 2,
+  Should = 3,
   /// Must be active regardless of external factors.
-  Must = 3,
+  Must = 4,
 };
 
 ItemActivity CombineActivity(ItemActivity a, ItemActivity b) {
@@ -1204,7 +1204,7 @@ static ItemActivity IsItemProbablyActive(
                                         aDisplayListBuilder, aUniformlyScaled);
 
       if (transformItem->MayBeAnimated(aDisplayListBuilder)) {
-        activity = CombineActivity(activity, ItemActivity::Should);
+        activity = CombineActivity(activity, ItemActivity::ShouldForAnimation);
       }
 
       return activity;
@@ -1258,9 +1258,9 @@ static ItemActivity IsItemProbablyActive(
         auto activity =
             HasActiveChildren(*aItem->GetChildren(), aBuilder, aResources, aSc,
                               aManager, aDisplayListBuilder, aUniformlyScaled);
-        // For masked items, don't bother with making children active since we
-        // are going to have to need to paint and upload a large mask anyway.
-        if (activity < ItemActivity::Must) {
+        // Only split the masked group for native content or required activity,
+        // not for animated transforms over blob content.
+        if (activity < ItemActivity::Should) {
           return ItemActivity::No;
         }
         return activity;
@@ -1345,8 +1345,8 @@ void Grouper::ConstructGroups(nsDisplayListBuilder* aDisplayListBuilder,
     auto activity = IsItemProbablyActive(
         item, aBuilder, aResources, aSc, manager, mDisplayListBuilder,
         encounteredActiveItem, uniformlyScaled);
-    auto threshold =
-        isFirst || isLast ? ItemActivity::Could : ItemActivity::Should;
+    auto threshold = isFirst || isLast ? ItemActivity::Could
+                                       : ItemActivity::ShouldForAnimation;
 
     if (activity >= threshold) {
       encounteredActiveItem = true;
